WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.070 --> 00:00:05.150
Speaker 1: We don't yet know exactly what
will happen today when it comes to the swearing

00:00:05.150 --> 00:00:09.640
in of lying Republican Congressman elect George
Santos.

00:00:09.640 --> 00:00:14.970
But it is now not only US criminal investigation
that Santos is under, having now found out

00:00:14.970 --> 00:00:22.630
where he is, Brazil has restarted its criminal
investigation of the very same Jorge Santos.

00:00:22.630 --> 00:00:24.289
This is unbelievable.

00:00:24.289 --> 00:00:28.369
The new or not unbelievable as we've learned
about this guy.

00:00:28.369 --> 00:00:34.940
The New York Times reports Brazilian authorities
will revive a fraud case against Jorge Santos.

00:00:34.940 --> 00:00:44.649
A 2008 court case had been suspended because
Brazilian law enforcement couldn't find Santos.

00:00:44.649 --> 00:00:50.350
When he takes his seat, he will do so under
the shadow of active investigations by federal

00:00:50.350 --> 00:00:52.460
and local prosecutors.

00:00:52.460 --> 00:00:55.489
But an older criminal case may be more pressing.

00:00:55.489 --> 00:01:01.500
This stems from a 2008 incident involving
a stolen checkbook, just like a pedestrian

00:01:01.500 --> 00:01:06.280
alleged criminal is this guy and the case
had been suspended for the better part of

00:01:06.280 --> 00:01:09.880
a decade, writes The New York Times, because
the police couldn't find him.

00:01:09.880 --> 00:01:16.369
Spokeswoman for the Rio prosecutor's office
said that with Santos, his whereabouts identified

00:01:16.369 --> 00:01:22.360
a formal request will be made to the DOJ to
notify him of the charges a necessary step,

00:01:22.360 --> 00:01:25.670
step after which the case will proceed with
or without him.

00:01:25.670 --> 00:01:29.960
The criminal case in Brazil was first disclosed
to the New York Times in a New York Times

00:01:29.960 --> 00:01:33.170
investigation that uncovered broad discrepancies
in his resume.

00:01:33.170 --> 00:01:34.720
I love that term.

00:01:34.720 --> 00:01:36.310
There were discrepancies.

00:01:36.310 --> 00:01:39.690
What is it he is accused of doing in Brazil?

00:01:39.690 --> 00:01:40.860
It's the following.

00:01:40.860 --> 00:01:46.610
A month before his 20th birthday, Santos entered
a small clothing store in the Brazilian city

00:01:46.610 --> 00:01:49.479
of Niteroi outside of Rio.

00:01:49.479 --> 00:01:54.720
He spent nearly 700 bucks using a stolen checkbook
and a false name.

00:01:54.720 --> 00:02:01.450
Court records show he admitted the fraud to
the shop owner in 2009, writing on Orkut,

00:02:01.450 --> 00:02:05.360
a popular social media website in Brazil,
quote, I know I screwed up, but I want to

00:02:05.360 --> 00:02:06.360
pay.

00:02:06.360 --> 00:02:09.940
In 2010, he and his mother told the police
he used the stolen checkbook of a man his

00:02:09.940 --> 00:02:14.550
mother used to work for and made fraudulent
purchases.

00:02:14.550 --> 00:02:17.920
So this this is just a horrible, horrible
person.

00:02:17.920 --> 00:02:21.690
And we don't exactly know what's going to
happen today, although he almost certainly

00:02:21.690 --> 00:02:24.220
will be seated.

00:02:24.220 --> 00:02:27.610
And you may even know about that by the time
today's show goes live.

00:02:27.610 --> 00:02:31.340
But we now have a situation where the Brazilian
government conveniently knows exactly where

00:02:31.340 --> 00:02:32.340
to find him.

00:02:32.340 --> 00:02:34.980
This is what Kevin McCarthy gets or whoever.

00:02:34.980 --> 00:02:40.090
Right, for refusing to expel this clown and
say, you know what?

00:02:40.090 --> 00:02:44.620
Too much dishonesty, too concerning, too disturbing
what he did.

00:02:44.620 --> 00:02:48.750
Now, Republicans are going to have to deal
with or stonewall and pretend it's not going

00:02:48.750 --> 00:02:49.840
on.

00:02:49.840 --> 00:02:51.620
What's going on with Jorge Santos?

00:02:51.620 --> 00:02:53.230
And it is quite a humiliating cloud.

00:02:53.230 --> 00:02:54.230
Now, will they care?

00:02:54.230 --> 00:02:55.400
I don't know.

00:02:55.400 --> 00:02:59.180
But we're talking about someone with outstanding
warrants in another country, essentially,

00:02:59.180 --> 00:03:02.230
and under criminal investigation in the United
States.

00:03:02.230 --> 00:03:08.150
If we want to be conspiratorial and we never
do, except sometimes we speculate.

00:03:08.150 --> 00:03:14.440
Is it possible that Santos made a promise
to McCarthy in McCarthy's fight for the speakership,

00:03:14.440 --> 00:03:18.950
which is as of this moment that I am recording
today, not a guarantee.

00:03:18.950 --> 00:03:21.340
We will know more about that within hours.

00:03:21.340 --> 00:03:27.180
Is it possible Santos promise to back McCarthy
if McCarthy promise not to try to get him

00:03:27.180 --> 00:03:28.870
kicked out of Congress?

00:03:28.870 --> 00:03:30.120
It's a question.

00:03:30.120 --> 00:03:33.340
It's not an assertion that I believe that
happened.

00:03:33.340 --> 00:03:37.150
But it is certainly a sensible question given
the circumstances.

00:03:37.150 --> 00:03:43.580
We don't yet know whether Kevin McCarthy will
have all the votes he needs to be speaker.

00:03:43.580 --> 00:03:49.680
And the question of loyalty between these
two afterwards seems very, very uncertain.

00:03:49.680 --> 00:03:55.290
The other aspect to this is there are increasingly
questions about the large amounts of money

00:03:55.290 --> 00:04:02.340
funneled through the Santos campaign that
suggested that he maybe had a source of funds.

00:04:02.340 --> 00:04:03.340
That was unclear.

00:04:03.340 --> 00:04:07.640
It didn't really line up with his fake claims
about where he used to work.

00:04:07.640 --> 00:04:09.470
I don't know.

00:04:09.470 --> 00:04:11.250
But once we now know.

00:04:11.250 --> 00:04:12.250
Although.

00:04:12.250 --> 00:04:13.920
This is petty in a sense.

00:04:13.920 --> 00:04:17.459
He was 19 years old in Brazil, talking about
$700.

00:04:17.459 --> 00:04:20.400
He clearly is willing to get up to some high
jinks.

00:04:20.400 --> 00:04:25.330
And if he was willing to do this at age 19,
what is it he may have been willing to do

00:04:25.330 --> 00:04:29.229
over the last year or two with regard to the
$700,000?

00:04:29.229 --> 00:04:33.400
That now is a question mark in terms of the
donation he made to his own campaign.

00:04:33.400 --> 00:04:36.419
A couple people e-mailed me and said, what
about extradition?

00:04:36.419 --> 00:04:40.009
Is it possible the U.S. would extradite him
to Brazil?

00:04:40.009 --> 00:04:41.009
I don't know.

00:04:41.009 --> 00:04:43.400
I wasn't able to talk to any lawyers about
this.

00:04:43.400 --> 00:04:48.259
We do have a treaty on extradition that has
been ratified by the U.S. and Brazil, signed

00:04:48.259 --> 00:04:53.389
in 1961, published in 1964.

00:04:53.389 --> 00:04:59.669
And I don't know how plausible it really is
to think Santos might be extradited to Brazil,

00:04:59.669 --> 00:05:05.080
but this is the epitome of the Republican
Party in 2023, grifters, alleged criminals

00:05:05.080 --> 00:05:09.610
and people who are going to spend the next
two years starting today trying to impeach

00:05:09.610 --> 00:05:12.820
Joe Biden, trying to investigate Hunter Biden.

00:05:12.820 --> 00:05:14.449
It starts today.

00:05:14.449 --> 00:05:17.991
And we we'd really better be ready to know
how to deal with it.

00:05:17.991 --> 00:05:19.901
It's not clear to me that the Democratic Party
is actually prepared.

